  ],
  "notes": "RELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{遺失物|いしつぶつ}→遺失物：15652_ishitsubutsu⟧ - lost property (formal/legal term)\n- ⟦{忘|わす}れ{物|もの}→忘れ物：01758_wasuremono⟧ - forgotten item (left behind, not dropped)\n- {拾|ひろ}い{物|もの} - found item\n\nUSAGE:\n{落|お}とし{物|もの} specifically refers to items accidentally dropped, while ⟦{忘|わす}れ{物|もの}→忘れ物：01758_wasuremono⟧ refers to items left behind or forgotten.\n\nLOST AND FOUND:\nIn Japan, lost items have a high return rate. Items can be reported or collected at police boxes (⟦{交番|こうばん}→交番：02879_kouban⟧) or dedicated {落|お}とし{物|もの}⟦センター→センター：03854_sentaa⟧ at train stations.",
